      "content": "A fever and those purple pinpricks could be a harmless viral infection or a heat rash, but you should monitor him closely. If he develops a rash, it could be a sign of something more serious like Henoch-Schönlein purpura, but it's rare. I recommend giving him acetaminophen for the fever, and if the rash doesn't spread or worsen, you can continue to watch him. But if you notice any changes, especially if he becomes lethargic or the rash spreads, you should seek medical attention immediately.",
